# Backend Conventions: packages/api

## Validation
- Every route parameter and query parameter must be validated in a
  dedicated validator middleware in `src/validators/`, not inline in
  the controller.
- On invalid input, respond with HTTP 400 and a body shaped exactly like
  `{ error: string }`. The message must be specific enough to say what
  was wrong (e.g. "id must be a positive integer"), not just "Bad Request".
- Follow the existing validator style in `route.validator.ts`: a
  named exported function, early return with `next()` on success.

## Error Handling
- A resource that isn't found returns HTTP 404 with
  `{ error: string }`, never a 200 with an empty or null body.
- Never swallow an error silently: every catch block either responds
  with a clear error status/body or re-throws.

## Logging
- Do not add `console.log` to controllers or validators. This codebase
  has no structured logger yet. If a change genuinely needs logging,
  flag it in the response instead of inventing a logging call.

## Testing
- Every new or changed endpoint needs a corresponding test in
  `tests/route.test.ts` (or a new file matching that naming pattern),
  covering at minimum: the success case, and one failure case.
- Never mark a task complete without running the relevant test file and
  showing the result.

## Data
- Never introduce fake or sample production data. This repo's sample
  data (`Route 12 – Riverside Loop`, `Route 4 – Harbor District`, etc.)
  is the only synthetic data allowed, and only in `src/data/` and test
  fixtures.
